# Every body language, every brace, every status class. Step through
# inject to watch each body handed to its grammar with its placeholders
# cut out, and paint to see the classes.

@host = api.example.com

### Typed by its first line, whatever the header says
# @name create
POST https://{{host}}/items
Content-Type: application/xml
X-Request-Id: {{$guid}}

{"looks": "like json", "so": "it is json"}

HTTP/1.1 201 Created
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": 1,
  "name": "{{name}}",
  "count": {{n}},
  "from": "{{create.response.body.$.id}}"
}

### Typed by the first line, placeholders left to the file dialect
POST https://{{host}}/items

{"name": "{{name}}", "tags": [{{tag}}, "fixed"]}

HTTP/1.1 304 Not Modified

### An xml opener with nothing to say it is HTML
GET https://{{host}}/page

HTTP/1.1 404 Not Found
Content-Type: text/html; charset=utf-8

<p>gone</p>

### HTML, revealed by its opener
GET https://{{host}}/page

HTTP/1.1 500 Internal Server Error

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en"><body><h1>{{title}}</h1></body></html>

### A form body, typed by its first pair
POST https://{{host}}/login

username={{user}}
&password=hunter2&remember=

HTTP/1.1 302 Found
Location: /home

### Braces that close no placeholder are text, everywhere
GET https://{{host}}/{{unclosed
X-Stray: }}stray{{
X-Quad: {{{{a}}}}
X-Nested: {{ {{b}} }}
X-Plain: survives

POST https://{{host}}/raw

{{unclosed
}} stray {
  {{c}}
}

### A wire message inside a response body, a form body inside that
GET https://{{host}}/echo

HTTP/1.1 200 OK
Content-Type: message/http

POST /echo HTTP/1.1
Host: {{host}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

a=1&b={{two}}
